cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you utilize the Optical-Mechanical Dual-Chassis architecture, Softmax Denominator Partitioning, or Wavefunction Dirac-Delta Collapse formulations in your research or systems, please cite this work as specified below."
title: "Deterministic Quantum Mechanics of Transformer In-Context Attention: Wavefunction Dirac-Delta Collapse via Optical-Mechanical Dual-Chassis"
abstract: >-
  Large language models (LLMs) governed by softmax-based self-attention inherently suffer from
  non-deterministic token drift, attention dispersion, and cumulative hallucination. In this paper,
  we formalize in-context attention dynamics through a quantum mechanical perspective, modeling the
  attention distribution as a statistical probability density over the discrete token Hilbert space.
  To eliminate attention drift without model fine-tuning or external orchestration wrappers, we
  introduce an In-Context Virtual Machine (ICVM) operating via an Optical-Mechanical Dual-Chassis
  control system. The Optical Chassis partitions the softmax partition function into an immutable
  static core basis and a dynamic token basis, inducing a potential energy barrier that contracts
  the continuous probability wavepacket into a deterministic Dirac-delta function centered precisely
  at the target attractor state. Concurrently, the Mechanical Chassis executes direct POSIX kernel
  system calls (stat()) to enforce monotonic physical byte and line growth.
